#**
 * Names the select of a picker of a macro parameter after the label that the macro editor displays for the parameter.
 * The macro editor gives the id "parameter-" followed by the parameter name to the field named after the parameter,
 * and labels it with a label for this id. The picker of recent XWiki versions (Tom Select) moves this label to its
 * text input, giving the label the id of the select followed by "-ts-label": the select, hidden but still read by the
 * screen readers, would have no name otherwise. Where the label isn't moved (Selectize, on older XWiki versions), the
 * select keeps its label, the reference to a missing id being ignored.
 *
 * @param $parameters the attributes of the select, holding the name of the macro parameter (name), to which the
 *   reference to the label is added; nothing is added when there is no name
 *#
#macro (pmLabelPickerAsParameter $parameters)
  #if ("$!parameters.name" != '')
    #set ($discard = $parameters.put('aria-labelledby', "parameter-${parameters.name}-ts-label"))
  #end
#end
